{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c43fff13-0cd7-4c72-a77e-03c32e02c470","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9838c23b909f3675","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-9snh8yf3/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E001.md","content":"# Llama Stack GA-readiness gap assessment\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the strategy's defining unknown: the full inventory\nof gaps between Llama Stack's current Tech Preview quality and the GA bar. TP\nfeedback is scattered across support tickets and no systematic GA-readiness\nassessment has been done. The assessment consolidates that feedback, inspects\nthe current API surface and error handling, examines upgrade-path and\nscale-limit evidence, and produces the definitive GA scope that all downstream\nLlama Stack hardening work is planned against.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Consolidate Tech Preview feedback from support tickets and other TP feedback\n  channels into a single gap inventory.\n- Audit the current state of the four GA-bar dimensions named by the strategy:\n  API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling.\n- Classify each inventoried gap by GA impact (blocks GA, should fix, defer)\n  with a stated rationale for inclusion in or exclusion from GA scope.\n- Produce the definitive GA scope document, replacing the strategy's\n  provisional estimate of the stability and hardening work's size.\n- Convert each in-scope gap into scoped downstream work (acceptance criteria\n  or work items) so the API-stability and support-posture efforts can consume\n  it directly.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written gap inventory exists covering all four GA-bar dimensions (API\n  stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with each gap\n  traceable to a TP feedback record, code/API inspection, or test evidence.\n- Every inventoried gap is classified as GA-blocking, non-blocking-but-in-scope,\n  or deferred, with a recorded rationale.\n- A definitive GA scope document is produced and is specific enough that the\n  API stability work and the production support posture work can be sized and\n  planned from it without re-deriving the analysis.\n- Follow-up items discovered during the assessment are recorded as scoped work\n  items or acceptance criteria rather than left as prose.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between current TP\n  quality and the GA bar, producing the definitive GA scope.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Scale-limit and upgrade-path verification require a live cluster running the\n  Llama Stack distribution; plan for cluster time during the assessment\n  window.\n- Sign-off of the definitive GA scope is a product decision — the technical\n  inventory this epic produces is the input to that decision.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41109,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9f91bb28960f45b","agent_id":"a90d80a7805d44139","session_id":"1137ef5d-6881-4563-aaa6-337da4612527","uuid":"d8f9d3fe-c8e8-4014-97bc-f09763da7359","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:09:05.251Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
