{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c43fff13-0cd7-4c72-a77e-03c32e02c470","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfc2e17838544509","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-9snh8yf3/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E002.md","content":"# Llama Stack API stability guarantee and tested upgrade path\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the published API stability guarantee for Llama Stack as\nrequired for GA: a versioned API surface, a deprecation policy, and a tested\nupgrade path from the last two Tech Preview releases. Enterprise customers\nwill not build production GenAI applications on APIs without stability\ncommitments, so this work converts the TP-era API surface into one a GA\nrelease can stand behind.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Version the published API surface of the Llama Stack distribution (the\n  OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the LlamaStackDistribution CRD surface).\n- Author and publish a deprecation policy describing how API changes are\n  announced, phased, and removed across releases.\n- Implement and automate verification of the upgrade path from each of the\n  last two TP releases to the GA release.\n- Remediate the API-stability gaps that the GA-readiness assessment assigned\n  to this surface (or record their explicit deferral with rationale in the GA\n  scope).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The published API surface is versioned, and the versioning scheme is\n  documented.\n- A deprecation policy is published covering announcement, phase-out, and\n  removal of API changes.\n- Automated upgrade verification exists and passes for upgrading a deployed\n  distribution from each of the last two TP releases: given a distribution\n  deployed at a prior TP release, when it is upgraded to the GA release, then\n  existing API consumers continue to function within the stability guarantee,\n  with any breaking changes covered by the deprecation policy.\n- Every API-stability gap assigned to this epic by the GA-readiness assessment\n  is either remediated or explicitly deferred with a recorded rationale.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): published API surface carries a stability guarantee — versioned\n  APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP\n  releases.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The size of this work is an estimate until the GA-readiness assessment\n  lands; this epic is gated on that assessment and its scope may be rewritten\n  by its findings.\n- API surfaces originate upstream (meta-llama/llama-stack); changes to\n  upstream API contracts may require midstream coordination or upstream\n  contribution.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41109,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9f91bb28960f45b","agent_id":"a90d80a7805d44139","session_id":"1137ef5d-6881-4563-aaa6-337da4612527","uuid":"4c818935-316c-4a34-882a-d081d625fabf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:09:11.590Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
