{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c43fff13-0cd7-4c72-a77e-03c32e02c470","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-92d79d017fb3b03b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-9snh8yf3/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E003.md","content":"# Llama Stack production support posture (SLOs, backport policy, supported configuration matrix)\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic puts the production support posture in place for Llama Stack GA:\ndocumented SLO targets, a backport policy, and a supported configuration\nmatrix. This is the operational commitment set that distinguishes a supported\nGA component from a Tech Preview one, and it is a distinct work product from\nthe API stability engineering — it is support-policy authoring plus\nconfiguration validation, reviewed by product and support stakeholders rather\nthan code review.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define and document SLO targets for the production support posture of\n  Llama Stack distributions.\n- Define and document the backport policy: which releases receive fixes, for\n  how long, and how backports are requested and delivered.\n- Build the supported configuration matrix enumerating the provider, storage,\n  and deployment configurations that are supported at GA, validated to the\n  extent the GA-readiness assessment's scale-limit and error-handling\n  findings require.\n- Incorporate the scale limits identified by the GA-readiness assessment into\n  the matrix as documented, supported limits.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- SLO targets are documented and reviewed by the accountable stakeholders.\n- The backport policy is documented, covering supported release lines, fix\n  duration, and the backport request path.\n- The supported configuration matrix exists, enumerates supported\n  configurations, and every entry is either validated or explicitly marked\n  with its validation status and limitations.\