{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bae2ecaa18e4b7c9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E003\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack production support posture (SLOs, backport policy, supported configuration\n4\t  matrix)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n6\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n7\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the assessment's scale-limit and error-handling findings change\n16\t    what must be covered, rewrite the supported configuration matrix and posture documents\n17\t    from the assessment's gap inventory; the SLO/backport/matrix deliverables remain\n18\t    the frame but their entries are re-derived.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 1\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Llama Stack production support posture (SLOs, backport policy, supported configuration matrix)\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic puts the production support posture in place for Llama Stack GA:\n41\tdocumented SLO targets, a backport policy, and a supported configuration\n42\tmatrix. This is the operational commitment set that distinguishes a supported\n43\tGA component from a Tech Preview one, and it is a distinct work product from\n44\tthe API stability engineering — it is support-policy authoring plus\n45\tconfiguration validation, reviewed by product and support stakeholders rather\n46\tthan code review.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- Define and document SLO targets for the production support posture of\n51\t  Llama Stack distributions.\n52\t- Define and document the backport policy: which releases receive fixes, for\n53\t  how long, and how backports are requested and delivered.\n54\t- Build the supported configuration matrix enumerating the provider, storage,\n55\t  and deployment configurations that are supported at GA, validated to the\n56\t  extent the GA-readiness assessment's scale-limit and error-handling\n57\t  findings require.\n58\t- Incorporate the scale limits identified by the GA-readiness assessment into\n59\t  the matrix as documented, supported limits.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- SLO targets are documented and reviewed by the accountable stakeholders.\n64\t- The backport policy is documented, covering supported release lines, fix\n65\t  duration, and the backport request path.\n66\t- The supported configuration matrix exists, enumerates supported\n67\t  configurations, and every entry is either validated or explicitly marked\n68\t  with its validation status and limitations.\n69\t- Scale limits identified by the GA-readiness assessment are reflected in the\n70\t  matrix as documented limits, and error-handling expectations from the\n71\t  assessment are covered by the posture documents.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-3 (P0): production support posture is in place — documented SLO\n76\t  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix.\n77\t\n78\t## Risks / Notes\n79\t\n80\t- SLO targets and the backport policy require product and support-organization\n81\t  sign-off; budget review time.\n82\t- The configuration matrix's scope is gated on the GA-readiness assessment's\n83\t  scale-limit findings and may be rewritten by them.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93cc13bea82195ae","agent_id":"a3c8344ca9bf30bea","session_id":"1137ef5d-6881-4563-aaa6-337da4612527","uuid":"abc2f447-383d-4b28-aa1e-d8327c0e8c56","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:12:01.