{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-887a57fb3f790030","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E004\n3\ttitle: TrustyAI guardrails as a supported Llama Stack integration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# TrustyAI guardrails as a supported Llama Stack integration\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic promotes safety guardrails via TrustyAI from an experimental flag to\n34\ta supported, documented integration for GA Llama Stack distributions. TrustyAI\n35\talready ships fairness/bias, drift, explainability, and guardrails services in\n36\tthe platform; the GA requirement is that wiring guardrails into a Llama Stack\n37\tdistribution is a supported configuration path with documentation, not an\n38\texperimental opt-in.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Replace the experimental-flag enablement of the TrustyAI guardrails\n43\t  integration with a supported configuration path for Llama Stack\n44\t  distributions.\n45\t- Validate the integration end to end: a Llama Stack distribution configured\n46\t  with TrustyAI guardrails applies guardrails as documented.\n47\t- Author integration documentation covering configuration, supported\n48\t  deployment shapes, and known limitations of the guardrails integration.\n49\t- Confirm the integration is covered by the platform's standard support\n50\t  posture (no experimental disclaimers on the supported path).\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A Llama Stack distribution can be configured with TrustyAI guardrails\n55\t  through a supported (non-experimental) configuration path.\n56\t- End-to-end verification passes: guardrails are applied to requests on the\n57\t  configured distribution as documented.\n58\t- Integration documentation exists covering configuration, supported\n59\t  deployment shapes, and limitations, with no experimental-status disclaimers\n60\t  on the supported path.\n61\t- The integration is listed as supported for GA distributions in the\n62\t  relevant support/configuration documentation.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-4 (P1): safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n67\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions.\n68\t\n69\t## Risks / Notes\n70\t\n71\t- The work spans TrustyAI (integration enablement, operator surface) and the\n72\t  Llama Stack distribution wiring; the TrustyAI team owns the integration\n73\t  deliverable and coordinates with the Llama Stack owning team on the\n74\t  distribution side.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93cc13bea82195ae","agent_id":"a3c8344ca9bf30bea","session_id":"1137ef5d-6881-4563-aaa6-337da4612527","uuid":"8fa6d965-bd41-4714-ad66-46b3e11893cf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:12:04.222Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-887a57fb3f790030","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
