{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c30d379a74f2bb9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack GA-readiness gap assessment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Llama Stack GA-readiness gap assessment\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's defining unknown: the full inventory\n30\tof gaps between Llama Stack's current Tech Preview quality and the GA bar. TP\n31\tfeedback is scattered across support tickets and no systematic GA-readiness\n32\tassessment has been done. The assessment consolidates that feedback, inspects\n33\tthe current API surface and error handling, examines upgrade-path and\n34\tscale-limit evidence, and produces the definitive GA scope that all downstream\n35\tLlama Stack hardening work is planned against.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Consolidate Tech Preview feedback from support tickets and other TP feedback\n40\t  channels into a single gap inventory.\n41\t- Audit the current state of the four GA-bar dimensions named by the strategy:\n42\t  API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling.\n43\t- Classify each inventoried gap by GA impact (blocks GA, should fix, defer)\n44\t  with a stated rationale for inclusion in or exclusion from GA scope.\n45\t- Produce the definitive GA scope document, replacing the strategy's\n46\t  provisional estimate of the stability and hardening work's size.\n47\t- Convert each in-scope gap into scoped downstream work (acceptance criteria\n48\t  or work items) so the API-stability and support-posture efforts can consume\n49\t  it directly.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A written gap inventory exists covering all four GA-bar dimensions (API\n54\t  stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with each gap\n55\t  traceable to a TP feedback record, code/API inspection, or test evidence.\n56\t- Every inventoried gap is classified as GA-blocking, non-blocking-but-in-scope,\n57\t  or deferred, with a recorded rationale.\n58\t- A definitive GA scope document is produced and is specific enough that the\n59\t  API stability work and the production support posture work can be sized and\n60\t  planned from it without re-deriving the analysis.\n61\t- Follow-up items discovered during the assessment are recorded as scoped work\n62\t  items or acceptance criteria rather than left as prose.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-1 (P0): GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between current TP\n67\t  quality and the GA bar, producing the definitive GA scope.\n68\t\n69\t## Risks / Notes\n70\t\n71\t- Scale-limit and upgrade-path verification require a live cluster running the\n72\t  Llama Stack distribution; plan for cluster time during the assessment\n73\t  window.\n74\t- Sign-off of the definitive GA scope is a product decision — the technical\n75\t  inventory this epic produces is the input to that decision.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af73dab549a307da","agent_id":"a574a11eee7d20c51","session_id":"1137ef5d-6881-4563-aaa6-337da4612527","uuid":"46249ace-919b-4b4b-9f21-b5494c74a6c9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:17:22.052Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c30d379a74f2bb9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
