ment SLO targets for the production support posture of\n51\t  Llama Stack distributions.\n52\t- Define and document the backport policy: which releases receive fixes, for\n53\t  how long, and how backports are requested and delivered.\n54\t- Build the supported configuration matrix enumerating the provider, storage,\n55\t  and deployment configurations that are supported at GA, validated to the\n56\t  extent the GA-readiness assessment's scale-limit and error-handling\n57\t  findings require.\n58\t- Incorporate the scale limits identified by the GA-readiness assessment into\n59\t  the matrix as documented, supported limits.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- SLO targets are documented and reviewed by the accountable stakeholders.\n64\t- The backport policy is documented, covering supported release lines, fix\n65\t  duration, and the backport request path.\n66\t- The supported configuration matrix exists, enumerates supported\n67\t  configurations, and every entry is either validated or explicitly marked\n68\t  with its validation status and limitations.\n69\t- Scale limits identified by the GA-readiness assessment are reflected in the\n70\t  matrix as documented limits, and error-handling expectations from the\n71\t  assessment are covered by the posture documents.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-3 (P0): production support posture is in place — documented SLO\n76\t  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix.\n77\t\n78\t## Risks / Notes\n79\t\n80\t- SLO targets and the backport policy require product and support-organization\n81\t  sign-off; budget review time.\n82\t- The configuration matrix's scope is gated on the GA-readiness assessment's\n83\t  scale-limit findings and may be rewritten by them.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af73dab549a307da","agent_id":"a574a11eee7d20c51","session_id":"1137ef5d-6881-4563-aaa6-337da4612527","uuid":"b364602c-ac4c-49e6-917f-293315640b0d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:17:24.